  "question": {
    "text": "The supply voltage to a room is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>120</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>V</mo></math>. The resistance of the lead wires is <math> <mrow> <mn>6</mn> <mi>&#160;&#937;</mi> </mrow> </math>. A <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>W</mo></math> bulb is already switched on. What is the decrease of voltage across the bulb, when a <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>240</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>W</mo></math> heater is switched on in parallel to the bulb?",
    "image": null
  },
